    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n82930" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πήληξ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ηκος</span>, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>helmet</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφὶ δέ οἱ κροτάφοισι φαεινὴ σείετο
					πήληξ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					13.805
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤμυσε κάρη πήληκι βαρυνθέν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					8.308
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱππόκομος π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				16.797
			</span></i>; old 
				Ep.
			 word, used by <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ra.</u>
				1017
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Top.</u>
				173b20
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> serpent's
				<i>crest</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hyps.Fr.</u>
				16(18).4
			</span></i>. (Commonly derived from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάλλω,
			πῆλαι</span>, from the nodding of the plume, <i><span class="en">
				Apollon.
				<u>Lex.</u>
			</span></i>, etc.)</div>
